<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    ==================== the Carver's ORDINARY trade ==========================

    Carving in this mod started as one thing: change someone's Color. That
    inverts the source. The wiki is explicit that crossing Colors is the rare
    extreme, and that what a Carver actually does all day is restoration -
    "regrowing or reattaching lost body parts, as well as cosmetic alterations
    and surgeries" - gated by being "prohibitively expensive to all colors
    except Gold". Expense, not rarity.

    That gap mattered because the armour now works: a pulse or recoil suit keeps
    its wearer alive through a fight and hands you back somebody extremely
    wounded and possibly missing pieces. Yellows patch them up. Violet Carvers
    make them whole again. Only the first half existed.

    CARVERS ARE VIOLETS, NOT YELLOWS. Worth stating because it is easy to assume
    otherwise: Yellows are the Society's physicians, and every Carver named in
    the source is a Violet - the caste engineered for artistry, working in flesh
    instead of stone. Enforced by RR_CarverWork below, which is checked in
    Bill.PawnAllowedToStartAnew.
  -->

  <!-- =============================== resFlesh ============================== -->
  <!--
    "A medicinal substance applied to the site of a wound to stop bleeding and
    help repair damaged tissue... a sprayable material made of microorganisms
    that scramble onto pores and tighten to make a flesh-like antibacterial
    coating."

    So it is a TENDING material, not a healing serum - which is the useful
    correction, because the obvious assumption is that it removes scars. It does
    not. It sits between industrial medicine (potency 1.00) and glitterworld
    (1.60) and is the thing a field medic sprays on somebody the armour just
    saved.
  -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="MedicineBase">
    <defName>RR_ResFlesh</defName>
    <label>resFlesh</label>
    <description>A canister of resFlesh. The contents are alive in the way a culture is alive - a suspension of engineered microorganisms that, sprayed across an open wound, crawl into the pores at its edges and lock together into a sealed antibacterial skin.

It closes a wound and keeps it closed, and it will not let anything grow in there. What it will not do is put back what was taken out. For that you need a Carver, and a Carver's fee.</description>
    <possessionCount>3</possessionCount>
    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RR_ResFlesh</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>0.85</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>32</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.35</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.4</Flammability>
      <!-- Between industrial 1.00 and glitterworld 1.60. Better at closing a
           wound than a suture kit, well short of an archotech nanite gel. -->
      <MedicalPotency>1.30</MedicalPotency>
      <MedicalQualityMax>1.15</MedicalQualityMax>
      <DeteriorationRate>2</DeteriorationRate>
      <WorkToMake>900</WorkToMake>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <MedicineIndustrial>1</MedicineIndustrial>
      <Neutroamine>2</Neutroamine>
    </costList>
    <recipeMaker>
      <workSpeedStat>DrugSynthesisSpeed</workSpeedStat>
      <workSkill>Intellectual</workSkill>
      <recipeUsers>
        <li>DrugLab</li>
      </recipeUsers>
      <researchPrerequisite>RR_Carving</researchPrerequisite>
      <skillRequirements>
        <Crafting>6</Crafting>
        <Intellectual>6</Intellectual>
      </skillRequirements>
      <bulkRecipeCount>4</bulkRecipeCount>
      <displayPriority>2100</displayPriority>
    </recipeMaker>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>ExoticMisc</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- ========================= restoration surgery ========================= -->
  <!--
    Both of these are Violet-only, both consume a Carver's kit, and both are
    expensive rather than dangerous - the opposite balance to a Color carving,
    which is cheap in materials and likely to kill you. That is the distinction
    the source draws and it is worth preserving in the numbers.
  -->

  <RecipeDef Abstract="True" Name="RR_RestoreBase" ParentName="SurgeryFlesh">
    <workAmount>18000</workAmount>
    <hideBodyPartNames>true</hideBodyPartNames>
    <anesthetize>true</anesthetize>
    <researchPrerequisite>RR_Carving</researchPrerequisite>
    <!-- Ordinary work for a Carver, so far safer than crossing a Color. -->
    <surgerySuccessChanceFactor>0.92</surgerySuccessChanceFactor>
    <deathOnFailedSurgeryChance>0.02</deathOnFailedSurgeryChance>
    <skillRequirements>
      <Medicine>10</Medicine>
    </skillRequirements>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimRising.RR_CarverWork" />
    </modExtensions>
  </RecipeDef>

  <RecipeDef ParentName="RR_RestoreBase">
    <defName>RR_RegrowBodyPart</defName>
    <label>regrow body part</label>
    <description>Grow a replacement for a part this person has lost, from their own tissue, and attach it. Slow, ruinously expensive, and the reason a Gold who loses a hand in the morning has one again by the end of the month.</description>
    <jobString>Regrowing body part.</jobString>
    <workerClass>RimRising.Recipe_RegrowPart</workerClass>
    <targetsBodyPart>true</targetsBodyPart>
    <!--
      Overrides the base's hideBodyPartNames. This recipe offers one entry per
      MISSING PART, and HealthCardUtility.GenerateSurgeryOption only appends
      " (left arm)" when hideBodyPartNames is false - inherited true, a pawn
      missing three parts showed three identical "regrow body part" entries.
    -->
    <hideBodyPartNames>false</hideBodyPartNames>
    <successfullyRemovedHediffMessage>{0} has regrown {1}'s {2}.</successfullyRemovedHediffMessage>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter>
          <thingDefs>
            <li>RR_CarvingKit</li>
          </thingDefs>
        </filter>
        <count>1</count>
      </li>
      <li>
        <filter>
          <thingDefs>
            <li>RR_ResFlesh</li>
          </thingDefs>
        </filter>
        <count>4</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <fixedIngredientFilter>
      <thingDefs>
        <li>RR_CarvingKit</li>
        <li>RR_ResFlesh</li>
      </thingDefs>
    </fixedIngredientFilter>
  </RecipeDef>

  <RecipeDef ParentName="RR_RestoreBase">
    <defName>RR_RepairScarring</defName>
    <label>repair scarring</label>
    <description>Cut out an old injury and rebuild the tissue around it so that nothing shows. A Peerless does not carry the record of a fight they won, and this is how that is arranged.</description>
    <jobString>Repairing scarring.</jobString>
    <workerClass>RimRising.Recipe_RepairScar</workerClass>
    <targetsBodyPart>false</targetsBodyPart>
    <workAmount>12000</workAmount>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter>
          <thingDefs>
            <li>RR_CarvingKit</li>
          </thingDefs>
        </filter>
        <count>1</count>
      </li>
      <li>
        <filter>
          <thingDefs>
            <li>RR_ResFlesh</li>
          </thingDefs>
        </filter>
        <count>2</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <fixedIngredientFilter>
      <thingDefs>
        <li>RR_CarvingKit</li>
        <li>RR_ResFlesh</li>
      </thingDefs>
    </fixedIngredientFilter>
  </RecipeDef>

  <!-- ================== the illegal one: crossing Colors =================== -->
  <!--
    "While illegal under The Society, carvers can also modify clients'
    reproductive systems to facilitate cross-color reproduction."

    This is the one Carver service the Society executes people over, and it is
    the counterpart to the global conception block in
    Source/RimRising/CasteRelationsPatches.cs - whose own comment already said
    that getting a child out of a mixed pairing takes a Carver, not permission.
    This is that Carver.

    EITHER partner having it is enough; the surgery makes one body compatible
    with the other rather than meeting in the middle.
  -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RR_CrossColorFertility</defName>
    <label>carved fertility</label>
    <labelNoun>carved fertility</labelNoun>
    <description>This person's reproductive system has been rebuilt by a Carver so that it will accept another Color. It is meticulous work and undetectable without looking for it, which is fortunate, because the Society's penalty for having had it done is death.</description>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.72, 0.60, 0.82)</defaultLabelColor>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <!-- Read by RR_CarveReproduction's incompatibleWithHediffTags, as vanilla's
         Sterilized tag is read by the sterilisation surgeries, so the surgery
         leaves the list once done instead of stacking a second copy. -->
    <tags>
      <li>RR_CarvedFertility</li>
    </tags>
  </HediffDef>

  <RecipeDef ParentName="RR_RestoreBase">
    <defName>RR_CarveReproduction</defName>
    <label>carve reproduction</label>
    <description>Rebuild a patient's reproductive system so that it will accept a different Color. The Society treats this as a capital crime, on the grounds that the Colors staying separate is the entire architecture, and anyone bridging it is attacking the architecture.</description>
    <jobString>Carving reproduction.</jobString>
    <workerClass>Recipe_AddHediff</workerClass>
    <addsHediff>RR_CrossColorFertility</addsHediff>
    <targetsBodyPart>false</targetsBodyPart>
    <workAmount>20000</workAmount>
    <!-- A capital crime in the setting, so it should read as one to any
         ideoligion that cares. -->
    <isViolation>true</isViolation>
    <!--
      EIGHTEEN, not vanilla's thirteen.

      Vanilla's own sterilisation surgeries sit at minAllowedAge 13, so the
      obvious move is to copy that number across. It is the wrong number here:
      this mod's standing rule is that nothing sexual is applied to anyone under
      18, and a reproductive modification is squarely inside that.

      This does NOT contradict docs/DESIGN.md 8e, which says COLOR carving has
      deliberately no age gate because the reference's central carving is
      performed on a teenager. Different surgery, different subject.
    -->
    <minAllowedAge>18</minAllowedAge>
    <incompatibleWithHediffTags>
      <li>Sterilized</li>
      <li>RR_CarvedFertility</li>
    </incompatibleWithHediffTags>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter>
          <thingDefs>
            <li>RR_CarvingKit</li>
          </thingDefs>
        </filter>
        <count>1</count>
      </li>
      <li>
        <filter>
          <thingDefs>
            <li>RR_ResFlesh</li>
          </thingDefs>
        </filter>
        <count>3</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <fixedIngredientFilter>
      <thingDefs>
        <li>RR_CarvingKit</li>
        <li>RR_ResFlesh</li>
      </thingDefs>
    </fixedIngredientFilter>
  </RecipeDef>

</Defs>
